{"slug":"sedum-album","plant":{"taxon":"Sedum album","family":"Crassulaceae","rank":"species","gbif_key":5362008,"wikidata":"Q253636","iucn":null,"gbif_occurrences":288492,"common_name":"white stonecrop","names":[{"source":"culpeper","name":"Stone-Crop, Prick-Madam, Or Small-Houseleek","monograph_id":"cul:293-stone-crop-prick-madam-or-small-houselee","confidence":"low","note":"Trailing stonecrop on walls and roofs; cooling, harmless virtues suggest S. album, not hot wall-pepper."}],"n_compounds":21,"top_compounds":[{"name":"2-phenethylamine","qid":"Q407411"},{"name":"quercetin","qid":"Q409478"},{"name":"isorhamnetin","qid":"Q416138"},{"name":"myricetin","qid":"Q951449"},{"name":"quercitrin","qid":"Q1649777"},{"name":"gossypetin","qid":"Q3036428"},{"name":"herbacetin","qid":"Q3073325"},{"name":"spiraeoside","qid":"Q7577713"}],"epmc_total":14,"trials":0,"claims":[{"concept_id":"fever","dsc":0,"cul":1,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":0,"lift":0.84,"evidence_tier":"unstudied"},{"concept_id":"hemorrhage","dsc":0,"cul":1,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":0,"lift":0.73,"evidence_tier":"unstudied"},{"concept_id":"hemorrhoids","dsc":0,"cul":1,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":0,"lift":0.99,"evidence_tier":"unstudied"},{"concept_id":"malaria","dsc":0,"cul":1,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":0,"lift":0.92,"evidence_tier":"unstudied"},{"concept_id":"plague","dsc":0,"cul":1,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":0,"lift":0.91,"evidence_tier":"unstudied"},{"concept_id":"poisoning","dsc":0,"cul":1,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":0,"lift":0.9,"evidence_tier":"unstudied"},{"concept_id":"scrofula","dsc":0,"cul":1,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":0,"lift":0.98,"evidence_tier":"unstudied"},{"concept_id":"skin_ulcers","dsc":0,"cul":1,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":0,"lift":0.98,"evidence_tier":"unstudied"}],"lead_score":null},"texts":{"cul:293-stone-crop-prick-madam-or-small-houselee":{"ref":"Culpeper, Complete Herbal: Stone-Crop, Prick-Madam, Or Small-Houseleek","headword":"Stone-Crop, Prick-Madam, Or Small-Houseleek","lang":"en","source":"culpeper","text":"It is under the dominion of the Moon, cold in quality, and something binding, and therefore very good to stay defluctions, especially such as fall upon the eyes. It stops bleeding, both inward and outward, helps cankers, and all fretting sores and ulcers; it abates the heat of choler, thereby preventing diseases arising from choleric humours. It expels poison much, resists pestilential fevers, being exceeding good also for tertian agues: You may drink the decoction of it, if you please, for all the foregoing infirmities. It is so harmless an herb, you can scarce use it amiss: Being bruised and applied to the place, it helps the king’s evil, and any other knots or kernels in the flesh; as also the piles.","spans":[{"start":171,"end":179,"concept_id":"hemorrhage","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":212,"end":219,"concept_id":"skin_ulcers","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":238,"end":243,"concept_id":"skin_ulcers","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":248,"end":254,"concept_id":"skin_ulcers","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":355,"end":361,"concept_id":"poisoning","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":376,"end":388,"concept_id":"plague","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":389,"end":395,"concept_id":"fever","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":427,"end":434,"concept_id":"malaria","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":636,"end":647,"concept_id":"scrofula","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":706,"end":711,"concept_id":"hemorrhoids","polarity":"therapeutic"}]}},"gloss":{"cul:293-stone-crop-prick-madam-or-small-houselee":{"171":"bleeding (inward / outward / of wounds)","212":"canker: spreading / eating ulcer","238":"sores, running sores","248":"ulcers (old, foul, running, fretting)","355":"resists / expels poison","376":"pestilence, pestilential fevers / sores","389":"fevers","427":"tertian ague (fever every third day)","636":"king's evil: scrofula","706":"piles: haemorrhoids"}},"images":[]}